DevOps Interview Preparation – Tool 7

Jenkins (Basics + Advanced) | 0–2 Years Experience

Jenkins is still one of the most widely used CI/CD tools in the industry.
Interviewers don’t expect you to know everything — but they do expect you to understand how Jenkins works in real projects.

📌 Focus: Jenkins Interview Questions (Mixed – Basics + Advanced)

• What is Jenkins and why is it used in DevOps?
• Difference between CI and CD in Jenkins context
• What is a Jenkins job?
• Difference between Freestyle and Pipeline jobs
• What is Jenkins Pipeline?
• Difference between Declarative and Scripted Pipeline
• What is a Jenkinsfile and where is it stored?
• Explain stages, steps, and agents
• What is a Jenkins agent/node?
• Master vs agent architecture
• How do you distribute builds across agents?
• What are Jenkins plugins?
• Most commonly used Jenkins plugins
• How do you manage credentials in Jenkins?
• What is Jenkins credential store?
• How do you secure Jenkins?
• How do you integrate Jenkins with GitHub/GitLab?
• How do you trigger Jenkins jobs automatically?
• Webhook vs polling
• What are build parameters?
• What are environment variables in Jenkins?
• How do you handle secrets in Jenkins pipeline?
• What is artifact in Jenkins?
• How do you store and share artifacts?
• How do you rollback a failed deployment using Jenkins?
• Common Jenkins issues faced by beginners
• Real-world Jenkins pipeline flow you used or studied

💡 Interview Tip:
If you can confidently explain:
 “Code commit → Jenkins build → Test →Artifact → Deploy”
you already sound like a production-ready DevOps engineer, even with 0–2 years of experience.
